&lt;td colspan=&quot;2&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary of proposed experiment:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:14px;&quot;&gt;Dr. Schrag will undergo a 5217-Alpha event, with the goal of establishing contact with, and learning the nature and intent of, SCP-5217-1.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td colspan=&quot;2&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reason for proposed experiment:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:14px;&quot;&gt;D-class tests have revealed that 5217-Alpha events cause no harm to the subject, but have failed to provide meaningful information regarding the contents of the dream experienced during 5217-Alpha events, or regarding the origins and intentions of SCP-5217-1. It is theorized, based on analysis of subject testimony, that D-class subjects&#039; reticence about their experience during 5217-Alpha events arises from their perception of that experience as a deeply personal moment of a romantic or sexual nature. As Dr. Schrag, in addition to being a loyal Foundation operative, is asexual and aromantic, it is believed that she is uniquely suited to attempt to make meaningful contact with SCP-5217-1.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:14px;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Approved&lt;/strong&gt;; no significant risks, significant potential rewards, and all that newfangled identity stuff everyone keeps going on about can actually be a help for a change. &amp;#8212;Site Director Wakefield&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
